Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:57:03 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 62/79] flashnext_mia lanes: verify windows and head levels
 timed as the shared rounds

The single-stream verify table (widths 1..window) and the head-level chains took one
dropped round and a median of 5 at boot. That table prices every round under the first
shared point (32 rows), so its noise moved 2- to 4-stream asks: one boot logged
12 rows at 63.6 ms and 16 rows at 52.6 ms; another 1 row at 33.8 ms, a third 44.2 ms.

Each verify width and head level now gets the shared rounds' timing: 4 untimed rounds of
the timed shape, the median of 9, the lower of 2 passes. Boot costs about 17 s more.
